% ============================================================================
% insect-parts.query.adj — a worked recall over the biology insect-parts library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what does the thorax
% bear?": it states no entomology fact of its own — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against
% the `insect_region_bears` rows and returns the value + the table's source/
% locator/trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the feature
% `legs_and_wings`, recall its region — thorax). A word that is not one of the
% three main body regions abstains honestly — the engine never invents a part.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli insect-parts.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "insect-parts.adj"

? insect_region_bears(head, $Bears)              % expect eyes_antennae_and_mouthparts
? insect_region_bears(thorax, $Bears)            % expect legs_and_wings
? insect_region_bears(abdomen, $Bears)           % expect digestion_and_reproduction
? insect_region_bears($Region, legs_and_wings)   % reverse bind — expect thorax
? insect_region_bears(tail, $Bears)              % expect abstain — an insect has no tail region; it is not one of the three main body regions
